<title>SPAIN: MOTOR RACING-ALESI QUICKEST IN JEREZ TESTING.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-ALESI QUICKEST IN JEREZ TESTING.</headline>
<dateline>JEREZ, Spain 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Frenchman Jean Alesi set the fastest time in his Benetton in testing on Monday for the world drivers' championship.</p>
<p>Alesi clocked a best time of one minute 21.01 seconds. Team mate Gerhard Berger was second fastest in 1:21.07.</p>
<p>World championship runner-up Jacques Villeneuve was third quickest in the new Williams FW19. He lapped in 1:21.25.</p>
</text>
